of whom a Contribution has been received by Licensor and subsequently
incorporated within the Work.

"Continuity Ledger" shall mean an append-only, cryptographically verified
record structure that persists state transitions and operational intent in
durable storage.

"Durable Record" shall mean a hardware-sealed, memory-immutable data structure
whose identity is mathematically bound to an RFC 8785 canonical hash.

"Zero Intent Loss (ZIL)" shall mean the architectural guarantee that valid user
inputs and transactions are persisted locally prior to external network
acknowledgement.

