4. Digital Continuity & Open Sovereignty Covenant
-------------------------------------------------
To ensure that software developed under this License remains faithful to the
Open Digital Continuity Standard (ODCS), any distribution of the Work or
Derivative Works must observe the following structural guarantees:

  a) Local Sovereignty: The software must allow complete local execution
     without requiring mandatory internet access, remote telemetry pings,
     or cloud gating for its core deterministic functions.

  b) Cryptographic Verification: Any modifications to the continuity ledger or
     durable record structures must maintain or enhance deterministic
     auditability (e.g., canonical RFC 8785 JSON serialization, SHA-256 Merkle
     proofs, and atomic WAL journaling).

  c) Data Portability: User data recorded via ODCS continuity constructs must
     remain exportable in open, documented formats, ensuring zero vendor lock-in
     and uninterrupted operational migration.

